{
  "summary": "This study investigates strategies to enhance magnesium-based hydrogen storage composites by optimizing thermodynamic and kinetic properties. The research reviews material modifications like catalysis, nanostructuring, alloying, and external field assistance to improve hydrogen storage capacity and reversibility. Key findings include improved gravimetric storage, reduced thermodynamic stability barriers, and accelerated sorption kinetics through tailored composite designs. These advances address critical challenges for practical hydrogen storage applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Enhanced gravimetric hydrogen storage capacity via composite engineering",
    "Reduced thermodynamic stability barriers through kinetic tuning",
    "Accelerated sorption kinetics using tailored material modifications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances the understanding of thermodynamic and kinetic optimization in magnesium-based hydrogen storage systems, providing a framework for designing efficient, reversible solid-state hydrogen storage materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated MALT1 expression in major depressive disorder (MDD) patients and MDD mouse models. Using blood samples from MDD patients and healthy controls, and unpredictable chronic mild stress to induce MDD in mice, researchers found elevated MALT1 expression in MDD patients. MALT1 inhibition with high-dose MI-2 reduced neural injury, improved behavioral abnormalities, and decreased inflammation in MDD mice, while lower doses showed minimal effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MALT1 expression was significantly elevated in MDD patients compared to healthy controls (median 3.41 vs. 1.10, P<0.001).",
    "High-dose MALT1 inhibition (35 mg/kg MI-2) reduced amygdala neuronal apoptosis and increased Nissl number in MDD mice.",
    "MALT1 inhibition decreased spleen Th17/Treg ratio, serum IL-17A, and TNF-α levels in MDD mice, improving behavioral outcomes."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study identifies MALT1 as a potential biomarker and therapeutic target for major depressive disorder, demonstrating that its inhibition alleviates neural injury, behavioral deficits, and inflammatory markers in preclinical models."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils expressing Nlrp3 and Il1b, which license pathogenic TH17 cells. After recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and Nlrp3-Il1b signaling license pathogenic TH17 cells during acute inflammation",
    "Chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist post-recovery, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite low-fat diet"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during narrow temporal windows can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a mechanism by which short-lived physiological changes impact long-term inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how hierarchical structural organization can intrinsically encode magnetic anisotropy in composite fibers. Researchers engineered aramid-silk-magnetite nanofibrils by growing magnetite nanoparticles within an aligned matrix, inspired by biomineralization. The fibers achieved high strength, modulus, and toughness (820 MJ m-3) while exhibiting tunable magnetic anisotropy from axial to radial easy axes. Collective dipolar coupling dominated magnetic anisotropy, enabling strain-mediated reconfiguration of magnetic properties and magnetoelastic actuation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Composite fibers with aramid-silk-magnetite structure achieved exceptional toughness (820 MJ m-3)",
    "Tunable magnetic anisotropy spanned axial to radial easy-axis configurations via structural relaxation",
    "Collective dipolar coupling dominated magnetic anisotropy by orders of magnitude over demagnetization effects"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a structural design principle for programming intrinsic magnetic anisotropy in mechanically robust magnetoelastic materials, enabling strain-controlled magnetic reconfiguration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated CENPT's role in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) progression. Using in vitro and in vivo experiments, the researchers identified CENPT as a critical regulator that activates the RAF/MEK/ERK pathway, promoting cell proliferation and metastasis. Transcriptomic analyses revealed CENPT correlates with increased regulatory T cells and immunosuppressive microenvironments. CENPT upregulates MIF secretion, which drives Treg differentiation and immunosuppression, suggesting CENPT inhibition could enhance immune checkpoint therapy efficacy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CENPT activates the RAF/MEK/ERK pathway to drive PDAC proliferation and metastasis",
    "CENPT correlates with elevated regulatory T cells and immunosuppressive tumor microenvironments",
    "CENPT upregulates MIF secretion, promoting Treg differentiation and immunosuppression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes CENPT as a key molecular driver in PDAC progression with dual roles in oncogenic signaling and immunosuppression, providing a potential target for combination immunotherapies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing bidirectional redox kinetics in lithium-sulfur batteries using a high-entropy complementary d-band center model. The approach involves designing multi-metal catalysts that align sulfur species' HOMO and Lusing the d-band center theory. The catalyst facilitates efficient capture, cascade conversion, and rapid desorption of polysulfides while suppressing the shuttle effect. Results show improved cycle stability and rate performance in Li-S batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Multi-metal catalysts align sulfur species' HOMO and LUMO via complementary d-band centers",
    "The catalyst enables a closed-loop pathway for efficient polysulfide conversion",
    "The design suppresses the shuttle effect and enhances cycle stability and rate performance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work extends d-band center theory to multi-metal systems, providing a mechanism for optimizing redox kinetics in lithium-sulfur batteries through tailored electronic structures."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the cellular sources of IFN-γ required for anti-PD-1 immunotherapy efficacy using genetic models to ablate Ifng in specific immune cell types. By assessing tumor growth and survival in MC38 and YUMMER1.7 models, the research demonstrated that CD8+ T cell-derived IFN-γ is essential for therapeutic response, while deletion in other cells (CD4+ Tconvs, Tregs, NK cells) did not impair efficacy. The findings indicate IFN-γ from CD8+ T cells promotes TCF1+ and CXCR3+ effector subsets and restricts terminal exhaustion during anti-PD-1 treatment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD8+ T cell-derived IFN-γ is necessary for anti-PD-1-mediated tumor control",
    "Deletion of Ifng in CD4+ Tconvs, Tregs, or NK cells does not affect anti-PD-1 efficacy",
    "CD8+ T cell IFN-γ drives TCF1+ and CXCR3+ effector T-cell subsets while limiting terminal exhaustion"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes CD8+ T cells as the obligate source of IFN-γ for anti-PD-1 immunotherapy, revealing a critical paracrine mechanism within the tumor microenvironment that underpins therapeutic response."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates suppressing electrode crosstalk in metal fluoride and sulfur batteries by designing a Na-rich nanoalloy (NaxSn) anode. The approach combines kinetic regulation via elevated Damköhler numbers and physical shielding through an ultrathin Na2O-rich solid electrolyte interphase. Results show 99.93% Coulombic efficiency over 200 cycles and 91.95% capacity retention after 1000 cycles at 0.5C in FeF2||NaxSn and S/C||NaxSn systems, demonstrating effective suppression of cation and anion crosstalk.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NaxSn anodes achieve 99.93% Coulombic efficiency over 200 cycles",
    "S/C||NaxSn systems retain 91.95% capacity after 1000 cycles at 0.5C",
    "The Na2O-rich solid electrolyte interphase non-selectively blocks cation and anion crossovers"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a dual mechanism for suppressing electrode crosstalk in high-energy batteries, enabling long-term cycling stability through spatiotemporally synergistic anode-cathode coupling."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the role of nerve growth factor (NGF) and its receptor TRKA in idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF) pathogenesis. Using Mendelian randomization, in vitro models with MRC5 cells, and murine pulmonary fibrosis models, the research demonstrates NGF-TRKA signaling activates fibroblasts via FAK/ERK pathway, induces endoplasmic reticulum stress, and promotes immune dysregulation. Key findings include NGF upregulation in IPF patients, CD4+CD39+FOXP3+ Treg involvement, and K-252a's antifibrotic effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NGF is significantly upregulated in peripheral blood of IPF patients",
    "CD4+CD39+FOXP3+ regulatory T cells show elevated expression in IPF and correlate with disease risk",
    "NGF-TRKA signaling via FAK/ERK pathway drives fibroblast activation and exacerbates pulmonary fibrosis"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies NGF-TRKA signaling as a mechanistic link between immune dysregulation and fibroblast activation in IPF, suggesting a novel therapeutic target for pulmonary fibrosis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing zinc-ion battery performance by designing a polymeric protective layer with amide and imidazolium groups. The amide groups stabilize Zn2+ transport via binding sites, while imidazolium groups create confined-water domains that regulate solvation. Water molecules act as transient coordination bridges during Zn2+ migration, improving single-ion conductivity by 6.55-fold and reducing hydrogen evolution by 79.1%. The approach extends cycling lifetimes to 2200 hours in symmetric cells and enables 4000 cycles with >85% capacity retention in full cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The polymeric layer with amide and imidazolium groups increases Zn2+ single-ion conductivity by 6.55-fold",
    "Hydrogen evolution rate is reduced by 79.1% due to confined-water domain regulation",
    "Zn//Zn symmetric cells achieve 2200-hour cycling with 1 mA cm-2 and 1 mAh cm-2"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a dual-functional interfacial strategy that enhances aqueous zinc-ion battery longevity through controlled water-mediated ion transport, advancing the design of stable, high-capacity grid-scale energy storage systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the role of ascites-derived interleukin-10 (IL-10) in advanced epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC) invasion. Using malignant ascites from 21 EOC patients, the researchers quantified IL-10 levels and assessed its correlation with clinical markers. In vitro and in vivo experiments demonstrated that ascites IL-10 promotes EOC cell migration and invasion via STAT3 and ERK1/2 signaling, with regulatory T cells and M2 macrophages as key IL-10 sources. IL-10 neutralization reduced tumor progression in vivo.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ascites-derived IL-10 levels correlated with serum cancer antigen 125 levels (r=0.553, p=0.014) but not ascites volume",
    "IL-10 significantly enhanced EOC cell migration and invasion through STAT3 and ERK1/2 signaling pathways",
    "Regulatory T cells and M2 macrophages in ascites were major sources of IL-10, driving pro-invasive tumor behavior"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes IL-10 as a critical immunosuppressive mediator in the EOC ascitic microenvironment that promotes tumor invasion through immune cell-tumor interactions, highlighting a potential target for microenvironment-modulating therapies in advanced ovarian cancer."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates phase evolution and crystallization kinetics in DMF-derived kesterite solar cells by introducing an ultrathin CdSe sacrificial layer at the Mo/precursor interface during selenization. The layer rapidly consumes to provide in-situ Se supply, overcoming surface transport delays and enabling early bottom selenization. This promotes CZTSSe formation, suppresses intermediate accumulation, and enhances grain growth. The approach achieved 14.78% certified efficiency, demonstrating a viable strategy for improving kesterite absorber quality through interface engineering.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ultrathin CdSe layer at Mo/precursor interface provides in-situ Se supply during selenization",
    "Early bottom selenization initiates conversion of Cu2SnSe3 intermediates to CZTSSe",
    "Redistributed Cd2+ reduces defect-assisted recombination and enhances carrier transport"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a method to coordinate phase evolution and crystallization kinetics in kesterite absorbers by enabling in-situ Se release at the buried interface, addressing a fundamental transport limitation in multinary chalcogenide solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines glutamine metabolic reprogramming in clear cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC), highlighting its role in remodeling the immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment and influencing immunotherapy response. It discusses molecular mechanisms like the VHL/hypoxia-inducible factor axis, MYC activation, and epigenetic regulation. Key processes include immune cell competition, impaired T-cell function, immunosuppressive cell expansion, and immune checkpoint upregulation. Therapeutic strategies targeting glutamine metabolism and candidate biomarkers are evaluated, emphasizing the need for patient selection in clinical applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Glutamine addiction in ccRCC drives immunosuppressive microenvironment remodeling through VHL/hypoxia-inducible factor axis and MYC activation",
    "Glutamine metabolism promotes immunosuppressive cell expansion and impaired T-cell function in ccRCC",
    "Therapeutic targeting of glutamine metabolism shows mixed clinical outcomes requiring precise patient selection"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides an integrated framework for understanding glutamine-driven immune modulation in ccRCC, advancing knowledge on metabolic reprogramming's role in immunotherapy resistance and guiding targeted therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates force dynamics in 3D epithelial tissues using a noninvasive method involving elastic polyacrylamide microbeads. The approach integrates microbeads into epithelia, enabling direct correlation between bead deformation and cytoskeletal architecture. Results show localized mechanical perturbations induce cytoskeletal remodeling without disrupting tissue polarity, with extracellular matrix composition influencing bead-tissue interactions. The technique reveals spatially heterogeneous force patterns at the cell-bead interface, extending traction force microscopy to 3D systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Localized mechanical perturbations trigger cytoskeletal remodeling while preserving tissue polarity",
    "Extracellular matrix composition determines bead-tissue interaction dynamics",
    "Quantitative analysis identifies sub-cellular scale force patterns at the cell-bead interface"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work extends traction force microscopy to 3D epithelia, revealing spatially heterogeneous force patterns critical for understanding tissue mechanics without invasive perturbations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used single-cell RNA sequencing to compare transcriptional profiles of airway CD4+ T cells in beryllium-exposed patients versus healthy controls. It identified 11 distinct cell clusters, including pathogenic CD4+ T cells with elevated expression of activation and immune regulatory genes (IFNG, TNF, TNFAIP3, CD74). Gene Ontology analysis showed upregulated immune activation pathways and downregulated metabolic processes in exposed patients, suggesting molecular mechanisms driving beryllium-induced pulmonary inflammation and potential biomarkers for chronic beryllium disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Beryllium-exposed patients exhibited pathogenic CD4+ T cells with elevated IFNG, TNF, TNFAIP3, and CD74 expression",
    "Gene Ontology analysis revealed upregulated immune activation pathways and downregulated metabolic processes in exposed patients",
    "Distinct transcriptional signatures including IFI27 and FABP4 were identified as potential biomarkers for chronic beryllium disease"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies specific transcriptional signatures in CD4+ T cells that may elucidate molecular mechanisms of beryllium-induced pulmonary inflammation, offering potential biomarkers and therapeutic targets for chronic beryllium disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing near-infrared (NIR) imager performance by reducing carrier recombination and dark current in Te-TeOx nanocrystalline-in-matrix films. The approach involves in situ bulk passivation via the oxide matrix, which modulates carrier transport to balance loss and extraction. Key results include reduced trap density, suppressed recombination, prolonged carrier lifetime, and tuned optical bandgap. The photodiodes achieve low dark current (9.70 nA cm-2), high detectivity (3.85 × 10^12 Jones), and ultralow detectable power (1.35 pW) for NIR detection, enabling monolithic integration with readout circuits for 256×256 focal-plane imagers.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reduced trap density and suppressed recombination in Te-TeOx films",
    "Tuned optical bandgap and interfacial offsets via controlled oxide incorporation",
    "Low dark current (9.70 nA cm-2) and high detectivity (3.85 × 10^12 Jones) for NIR photodetection"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a strategy for low-noise NIR imaging through in situ bulk passivation and carrier transport modulation in Te-TeOx films, advancing photodetector design for applications requiring high sensitivity and low noise in the visible to NIR spectrum."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cytotoxic CD4+ T cells expressing KLRG1 in cancer contexts. Using murine tumor models and human ccRCC specimens, researchers identified KLRG1+ Tconv as terminally differentiated cells with immunosuppressive functions, including IL-10 production and granzyme B secretion. These cells, derived from FoxP3-negative exTregs, maintain suppressive activity despite losing FoxP3. KLRG1-targeted depletion showed superior efficacy over blockade in slowing tumor growth.",
  "key_findings": [
    "KLRG1+ Tconv exhibit a terminally differentiated phenotype with immunosuppressive functions",
    "KLRG1+ Tconv derive from FoxP3-negative exTregs and retain suppressive capacity",
    "KLRG1-targeted depletion outperforms blockade in reducing tumor growth"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work reveals a conserved pathway of CD4+ T cell plasticity in tumors, demonstrating that cytotoxic KLRG1+ T cells can originate from Tregs and maintain immunosuppressive function without FoxP3, offering insights into immunotherapeutic strategies targeting T cell exhaustion."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines smart luminescent materials (SLMs) that convert external stimuli into programmable photonic outputs. It integrates molecular photophysics with structural dynamics to modulate emission properties like intensity, wavelength, polarization, and lifetime. The study covers solution-phase systems, solid-state materials, hydrogels, chiral systems, and lanthan: doped nanoparticles, highlighting how stimuli regulate excited states and molecular conformations. Key applications include information security, wearable electronics, and biophotonics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SLMs enable precise modulation of emission intensity, wavelength, polarization, and lifetime through external stimuli",
    "Stimuli regulate excited-state electronic structures and molecular conformations to achieve adaptive luminescent behaviors",
    "Emerging strategies for stimuli-responsive circularly polarized luminescence and intelligent photon conversion are highlighted"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review advances understanding of how molecular-level control mechanisms translate to dynamic optical functionalities in smart luminescent materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the role of CD8 regulatory T cells (CD8 Tregs) in natural intraepithelial lymphocyte (IEL) development. Using mouse models, researchers identified CD8 Tregs expressing Ly49 and Helios, which were linked to intestinal IELs. Blocking intestinal trafficking increased splenic CD8 Treg frequency, and transferred CD8 Tregs generated IELs. TCRs from splenic CD8 Tregs deterministically directed IEL development, while Helios was dispensable for this process.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD8 regulatory T cells in the spleen are linked to natural intraepithelial lymphocytes in the small intestine",
    "Blocking intestinal trafficking increases splenic CD8 regulatory T cell frequency",
    "T cell receptors from splenic CD8 regulatory T cells deterministically direct natural intraepithelial lymphocyte development"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that T cell receptors from splenic CD8 regulatory T cells directly instruct the development of natural intraepithelial lymphocytes, revealing a shared developmental program between these immunoregulatory cell types."
}

{
  "summary": "This review explores ambient-pressure X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (APXPS) for in situ analysis of gas/solid/liquid interfaces in small-molecule electrocatalysis. It categorizes three electrochemical APXPS approaches: quasi-in situ XPS, thin-electrolyte-film (dip-and-pull) APXPS, and membrane-based APXPS. The study highlights how APXPS enables direct correlations between catalyst evolution, reaction intermediates, and interfacial environments under operating conditions, advancing understanding of structure-activity relationships in small-molecule electrolysis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "APXPS provides surface-sensitive chemical state information at working interfaces during electrocatalysis",
    "Three distinct electrochemical APXPS configurations are identified for probing gas/solid/liquid interfaces",
    "APXPS enables direct correlation of catalyst evolution with reaction intermediates under operating conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes APXPS as a critical tool for resolving dynamic interfacial processes in small-molecule electrocatalysis, enabling structure-intermediate-environment relationships under realistic operating conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated epigenetic mechanisms suppressing Smad7 expression in fibrostenotic Crohn's disease (CD) to understand intestinal fibrosis pathogenesis. Researchers analyzed subepithelial myofibroblasts and muscularis smooth muscle cells from CD patients, revealing DNMT1-dependent promoter hypermethylation and miR-21-mediated degradation of Smad7 mRNA. Additionally, Smurf1/2 promoted proteasomal degradation of acetylated Smad7. Inhibition of miR-21 or demethylation restored Smad7 expression, reducing profibrotic signaling. These findings highlight how epigenetic and post-translational mechanisms collectively drive TGF-β1-mediated fibrosis in CD.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNMT1-dependent promoter hypermethylation silences Smad7 in fibrostenotic CD myofibroblasts",
    "miR-21 mediates Smad7 mRNA degradation via pSmad3 signaling",
    "Smurf1/2 promotes proteasomal degradation of acetylated Smad7 protein"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies epigenetic and post-translational mechanisms that suppress Smad7 in Crohn's disease fibrosis, providing mechanistic insights into TGF-β1 dysregulation and potential therapeutic targets for intestinal fibrosis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the controlled growth of non-layered NiO nanosheets on MoS2 using coupled external fields. By depositing amorphous NiOx onto monolayer MoS2 and visualizing in situ via environmental transmission electron microscopy, the research demonstrates electron beam-induced decomposition of NiOx into mobile species that nucleate on MoS2. The findings reveal interface-directed epitaxial growth mechanisms where Ni-O units attach preferentially at the interface, forming one-dimensional fronts through oriented attachment, interfacial fusion, and defect-mediated reconstruction, ultimately achieving single-crystalline NiO structures.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Electron beam decomposition of amorphous NiOx generates mobile species that nucleate on MoS2",
    "Ni-O units preferentially attach at the NiO/MoS2 interface to form one-dimensional growth fronts",
    "Oriented attachment proceeds via interfacial fusion and defect-mediated reconstruction, yielding single-crystalline NiO"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes an in situ method to resolve nucleation and growth pathways for non-layered 2D metal oxides, enabling precise control over their atomic-scale structural evolution through interface-directed mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a 30-parameter spectral flow cytometry panel to deeply phenotype peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) from African green monkeys and baboons. The panel profiles key immune subsets including B cells, NK cells, dendritic cells, monocytes, T cells, memory phenotypes, functional cytokines, activation markers, and regulatory T cells in both steady-state and mitogen-stimulated conditions. The approach addresses the limited immunophenotyping tools for non-human primates, particularly for HIV and pertussis research applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A 30-parameter spectral flow cytometry panel was created for deep immunophenotyping of African green monkey and baboon PBMCs",
    "The panel profiles major immune subsets including B cells, NK cells, dendritic cells, monocytes, T cells, memory phenotypes, functional cytokines, activation markers, and regulatory T cells",
    "The panel enables analysis of immune responses in steady-state and mitogen-stimulated conditions for both species"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a versatile immunophenotyping tool for non-human primates, advancing the ability to study immune responses in critical disease models like HIV and pertussis without human intervention."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of amplifying weak biological signals by developing ambipolar fiber amplifiers using a novel polymer. The research fabricated a single-component semiconductor fiber platform with balanced p- and n-type transport, achieving record-high charge transport metrics. The amplifiers demonstrated high voltage gain (up to 150 V/V) and low operating voltages (0.5 V), enabling high-fidelity electroencephalogram amplification and cortisol detection at 3.7 fM.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Record-high charge transport metrics in ambipolar polymer fibers",
    "High voltage gain (up to 150 V/V) and low operating voltages (0.5 V)",
    "High-fidelity electroencephalogram amplification and cortisol detection at 3.7 fM"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a general ambipolar fiber platform for integrated bioelectronic amplification and sensing, advancing the field of highly sensitive biosignal detection through scalable, conformal amplification solutions."
}
